WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.395
ALEX: Because the personalization only
works if the device knows nobody else is

00:00:02.395 --> 00:00:04.791
ALEX: looking.

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:07.360
JAMIE: And we don't know how it handles
that. Does it blank the

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.819
JAMIE: screen when you step away? Does
it require you to walk up

00:00:09.819 --> 00:00:12.278
JAMIE: before it shows anything
sensitive?

00:00:12.363 --> 00:00:15.236
RUFUS: Apple hasn't specified that in
what's been released. Which is a notable

00:00:15.236 --> 00:00:18.108
RUFUS: gap for a device built around the
idea that your household data

00:00:18.108 --> 00:00:20.981
RUFUS: is private to you.

00:00:21.161 --> 00:00:23.953
ALEX: It could be that this is the thing
that makes or breaks

00:00:23.953 --> 00:00:26.744
ALEX: the product in actual use. Not the
face recognition itself — but

00:00:26.744 --> 00:00:29.536
ALEX: what the device does with your
information when you're not the one

00:00:29.536 --> 00:00:32.327
ALEX: standing there.
